<title>NETHERLANDS: NEDERLANDSE WATERSCHAPSBANK TO REDEEM BOND EARLY.</title>
<headline>NEDERLANDSE WATERSCHAPSBANK TO REDEEM BOND EARLY.</headline>
<dateline>THE HAGUE 1997-03-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Dutch local authorities bank, Nederlandse Waterschapsbank NV, said on Thursday it would redeem its 100 million guilder 6.5 percent 1986 bond due between 2002 and 2006 at a price of 103 percent from April 15.</p>
<p>It said from that date the bonds would stop paying interest and they would be delisted from the Amsterdam Stock Exchange.</p>
<p>-- Amsterdam newsroom +31 20 504 5000, Fax +31 20 504 5040</p>
